+# Operations Manager memorandum found; the underlying dialogue remains unacquired
+
+October30,2026. Existing B129 /PD01–PD04 /FAA01–FAA04 and REC03source-coverage queue. **The acquired AWA940memorandum names NewYorkOperationsManagerInCharge (OMIC),1230–1344UTC—the position/range sought from the earlier Item16list.** This is a closer candidate counterpart, not proof of the exact delivered enclosure, source tape or complete transcript. Its two pages contain descriptive memorandum text, a role/abbreviation legend and footer material; no visible time-coded dialogue appears. No missing-audio duration or deliberate omission is established.
+
+## Exact source and actual scope
+
+NARA [7599164 /AWA940](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7599164); [direct PDF](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialz/dc-metro/rg-237/7419198-9-11-faa/5-Miscellaneous/c-Transcripts/5-AWA-940-Memorandum-Full-Transcript-New-York-ARTCC.pdf). Retrieved2026-10-30T16:55:23UTC, HTTP200,application/pdf, **31,742bytes /two pages**, SHA256 **97baabe1e23b268da2c9e02d6510b7c19bd65234e22f3e1cb8b1bdeb210fe530**. Both images were inspected in full. The unchanged original is preserved separately from these notes; raw PDF, full extraction, staff/signature/contact information and private case material are excluded from this derivative. No repeated search or new broader corpus review occurred. Native Word, signing/delivery, source channel/copy and clock authentication remain incomplete.
+
+Physical1subject/extractionlines8–10 identifies **Full Transcript; UAL175**. Line12names **ZNY-ARTCC-148**; line13prints **February4,2002**. Lines16–18declare **NewYorkCenterOperationsManagerInCharge (OMIC), September11,2001,1230–1344UTC**. Physical2line10references **UAL175_MEMO.doc**; the footer's date token on line11is **09/25/2001**. Other personal/contact portions of that footer are not republished. Both pages retain visible pagination/masthead placeholder text. [Exact fields, source relationships and scope](SOURCE-RECORD.json).
+
+## A reference to a full transcript is not the transcript body
+
+The catalog calls this a **memorandum**. Its heading and declarative range refer to a Full Transcript; the acquired two-page entity does not show that conversation. It could be intended descriptive/cover material, a form/template output, an incomplete export or a selected part of a larger assembly. **Those alternatives remain untested.** Do not choose an omission explanation from the absent dialogue or certify completeness merely from the heading.
+
+The role legend distinguishes **ZNY OMIC**, **CC-NOM**, and other identifiers. It pairs CC-NOMwith the AirTrafficControlSystemCommandCenter's NASOperationsManager and Huntresswith the24thAirDivision. A role/abbreviation entry is not a timestamped call record, proof a named organization joined a particular bridge, or an independent clock anchor. This also gives no demonstrated mapping from a generic NOMaudio filename to the listed NewYorkOMICrecording. Actual channel/copy/certification and dialogue remain necessary.
+
+The [earlier Item16source](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/62a102da31cc82a7216dc41e60bed185a11c8d45/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-response-labels-2026-10-30/README.md), physical15/printed8and16/printed9, lists OperationsManager rerecordings **1230–1331and1331–1340UTC** against a full-transcript label **1230–1344UTC**. AWA940now supplies a directly acquired released memorandum declaring the latter position/range, but its source-copy/certification join is not established. It does not demonstrate that actual audio ends at1340or explain the earlier four-minute end-label difference. Additional Item20material remains a possible source. No audio was acquired, played, transcribed, decoded, aligned or repaired in this step.
